  "articleBody": "Clean, flat drywall joints are what make fresh paint and trim look sharp. If you are planning an interior renovation, knowing how taping and mudding work helps you hire the right team.\n\nKey Benefits of Proper Finishing\nCorrect taping embeds strong paper or fiberglass reinforcement into joints, stopping seasonal shifts from cracking your walls and ensuring flat seams under harsh lighting.\n\nProcess Breakdown\nThe process starts by applying a thin bedding coat of joint compound into joints and over fastener dimples. Tape is centered and embedded smoothly to eliminate air pockets. Once dry, wider finish coats are applied, feathering edges outward. After thorough drying and light sanding, surfaces are primed to seal the porous mud.\n\nReal Examples\nFinishing a finished basement or garage requires distinct compounds and drying schedules depending on room temperature and ventilation. Premixed drying compounds often need a full 24 hours between coats, whereas setting compounds harden faster for specific base layers.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process\nExpect multiple visits or drying intervals between coats rather than a rushed single-day job. Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC provides hands-on drywall finishing and painting across the Denver metro. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your remodel.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
